 "description": "Returns the full content of a single document \u2014 invention, patent application, strategy, or report \u2014 or a meeting identified by its search result ID. A meeting returns a Markdown snapshot of its canvas text notes and all stored transcript sessions, with speakers, timestamps, and session status. A document has several texts across its lifecycle; a bare document ID returns the most advanced one (the newest application text, else the priority draft, else the innovation description), and the response lists every part with its own ID, such as document:<id>#priority_draft or document:<id>#application_text:<revisionId>. Pass a part ID to read that text instead. Saved own records can also return a structured family overview, including the current saved links and a per-record refresh assessment for readback after updates. Focused questions support include: [\"claims\"], [\"description\"], [\"abstract\"], or a combination. For a known document ID, mode: \"outline\" discovers native section availability without full text. Filtered content is returned in bounded pages with source/revision and content_version attribution. retrieval.next_cursor continues the same ID and include while has_more is true; stale cursors require restarting. Blocks identify oversized continuations with continued/continues; fragments with the same block_id concatenate directly. Missing/unknown sections and import warnings describe stored content, separately from page completeness. This reads stored content without importing, repairing, or contacting a patent provider. Omitting all options returns legacy full content.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "properties": {
   "cursor": {
    "description": "Opaque next_cursor for the same ID, include and content version; requires include",
    "maxLength": 2048,
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "id": {
    "description": "The search result ID, such as meeting:<id>, or a document identifier",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "include": {
    "description": "Native sections to retrieve; omission preserves legacy full fetch unless mode is outline",
    "items": {
     "enum": [
      "claims",
      "description",
      "abstract"
     ],
     "type": "string"
    },
    "maxItems": 3,
    "minItems": 1,
    "type": "array"
   },
   "mode": {
    "description": "outline discovers section availability; content requires include",
    "enum": [
     "outline",
     "content"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "id"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
